  "method": "Guadeloupe archipelago: Basse-Terre (Réserve Cousteau and Pigeon Islets, Bouillante to Pointe-Noire), Grande-Terre, Les Saintes, Marie-Galante, La Désirade and Petite-Terre. The Parc national de la Guadeloupe publishes no machine-readable list of the reserve's moorings or dive sites (searched in French; the park's pages name only the fixed moorings in general), so no official list is used; the Guadeloupe Islands tourism board page (lesilesdeguadeloupe.com) counts as one list. Operator lists read in French: Centre des Ilets (Bouillante), Les Heures Saines (Malendure; its reserve, wrecks, off-park and Sec Pâté pages), Atlantis Plongée, Archipel Plongée (wrecks page only), Bleu Passion (wreck dives page only), plus Pisquettes and La Dive Bouteille (Les Saintes; both publish their site maps as images or script-rendered pages, so only their named Sec Pâté is readable) and the Manbalaou club on Marie-Galante (site list not published as text). A site is counted when named on at least two independent lists; sites on one list are kept as excluded. Alternate names are merged (Pointe à Lézard on Atlantis is Pointe Lézarde). The wreck Gustavia lies at 40 m, the recreational limit, and is counted. Grande-Terre, Marie-Galante, La Désirade and Petite-Terre are thin: their sites appear only on the tourism board page, so they are excluded as single-list. Aggregators (divessi, diveplannerpro, manawa, blogs) were read for leads only. Counted 2026-10-14.",
